From 3fa9b6d1afa6dd42513a24db4028489393c147ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 06:46:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][PlayerInfo] A picture setting that the video's own
 choice overrode is not said, counted or put back

With "HDR10 as Dolby Vision, measured" on, an HDR10 film played with
"HDR output (this video)" set to play it without Dolby Vision went out
as HDR10, as chosen, and the overview page of the player information
said "Normal, without Dolby Vision", with the reason that another output
was chosen; but its heading still said "Your settings change the picture
from the film: made Dolby Vision", with "Picture settings changed: 1"
and a Restore button that would have reset a setting that had changed
nothing of that video.

PictureDefaults.h counted a setting that makes a video Dolby Vision
(videoscreen.hadesdvfromhdr10, hadesdvfromhdr10plus, hadeshlgasdv) for
every HDR10, HDR10+ or HLG video, whether or not the video went out as
Dolby Vision, and whether the setting or the video's own choice decided
it. Such a setting changes the picture only where it made the video
Dolby Vision: the video goes out as Dolby Vision, made from what that
setting makes it from, and its own choice is Automatic.

- New scopes MADE_DV_HDR10, MADE_DV_HDR10PLUS and MADE_DV_HLG, one for
  each of those settings; ScopeOf() gives them only for a video sent as
  Dolby Vision whose choice is Automatic, by what its Dolby Vision is
  made from (hades.dv.origin, MadeDolbyVisionBy(): measured,
  hdr10plus/hdr10pluscurve, measuredhlg; never measuredauto, measured
  because the output cannot send HDR10, which no setting decides). So an
  HDR10+ video made Dolby Vision from its HDR10+ names (and resets) the
  setting of HDR10+ only, not the one of HDR10.
- An HDR video that goes out as SDR (its choice "As SDR", or "HDR as
  SDR") has no scope: no setting of HDR output reaches its picture.
- The player information passes the origin and whether the choice is
  Automatic (DVBRIDGE::GetOutputChoice()); kodi.log's line of the
  picture settings (CLinuxRendererGLES::LogPictureSettings()) the same,
  through DVBRIDGE::MadeDolbyVisionFromNow(), and an HDR picture that
  the renderer maps to SDR names none.

What counts, the line, the count and the ids that the button resets
come from the same list, so all three follow. Decided where the page is
published (twice a second at most, while it is shown), never per frame.
